{#
The settings tree: areas that fold open, the pages in each, and a filter above
them that also finds the cards on every page (#569).

Variables (from SettingsController::page()):
    navigation   list<SettingsArea>, every area and page that can exist
    currentPage  SettingsPage being shown
    currentArea  SettingsArea it belongs to
    section      currentPage.slug, the name the rest of index.html.twig uses

THE TREE IS SERVER-RENDERED AND WORKS WITHOUT SCRIPT. Each area is a <details>,
open when it holds the current page, so the page you are on is always in view
and the others are one click away. settings/nav_controller.js only adds the
filter and the phone's show/hide; with it broken the tree is still a tree.

EVERY CARD IS IN THE MARKUP, hidden. The filter shows the cards that match
under their page, which is the third level the old navigation did not have:
somebody looking for "time zone" gets the card, not a page called "Language &
region" they would have had to guess. Rendering them here rather than fetching
the palette's index keeps the filter instant and gives the cards real links.
About eighty hidden rows; cheaper than a request per keystroke and than a
second copy of the matching rule.

Two pages are conditional, as they were as flat entries:

  • Account health shows while there is something wrong, or while it is open.
    The banner above the tree says the same thing louder; the entry is how the
    page stays reachable from the tree while you are on it — a tree with no
    entry for the open page has nothing to mark aria-current on.
  • Assistant shows where the administrator has switched an AI feature on
    (ai_settings_available() asks THEIR switches only, so somebody who turned
    all three of their own off can still find the page that turns them back
    on), or while it is open.

Every area folds the same way, Integrations included, although it holds one
page: it was drawn as a plain link at first, and one row in eight behaving
differently read as a different kind of thing rather than as a shortcut.
#}
{% set attention = accountHealth.attention %}
{% set aiOn = ai_settings_available() %}
{% set navActive   = 'flex items-center gap-2 px-2.5 py-1.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium bg-raised text-ink' %}
{% set navInactive = 'flex items-center gap-2 px-2.5 py-1.5 rounded-lg text-sm text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover transition-colors' %}

<div class="settings-nav min-w-0"
     data-controller="settings--nav"
     data-settings--nav-keyword-label-value="{{ 'settings.search.keyword'|trans }}">
    {# Below md the tree is a panel behind this button, which names where you
       are. The old navigation was a strip of twenty-nine wrapping pills there,
       taller than most of the pages it led to. #}
    <button type="button"
            class="md:hidden w-full flex items-center gap-2 px-3 h-10 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface text-sm text-ink"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="settings-tree"
            data-settings--nav-target="toggle"
            data-action="settings--nav#toggle">
        <i class="{{ currentArea.icon }} w-4 text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-left">
            {{ currentArea.labelKey|trans }} › <span class="font-medium">{{ currentPage.labelKey|trans }}</span>
        </span>
        <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down text-xs text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>

    <div id="settings-tree" class="hidden md:block mt-2 md:mt-0" data-settings--nav-target="panel">
        <div class="relative mb-3">
            <label for="settings-filter" class="sr-only">{{ 'settings.search.label'|trans }}</label>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-xs text-ink-faint pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <input type="search"
                   id="settings-filter"
                   autocomplete="off"
                   spellcheck="false"
                   placeholder="{{ 'settings.search.placeholder'|trans }}"
                   class="w-full h-9 pl-8 pr-14 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface text-sm text-ink placeholder:text-ink-faint focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent/40"
                   data-settings--nav-target="input"
                   data-action="input->settings--nav#filter keydown.esc->settings--nav#clear">
            {# The palette's shortcut, named where people look for search. The
               controller writes ⌘K over this on a Mac. #}
            <kbd class="absolute right-2 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 px-1.5 rounded border border-line text-[10px] text-ink-faint font-sans pointer-events-none"
                 data-settings--nav-target="shortcut">Ctrl K</kbd>
        </div>

        {% if attention %}
            <a href="{{ path('app_settings_page', { page: 'health' }) }}"
               class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border text-xs
                      {{ attention.tone == 'danger' ? 'border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10 text-red-700 dark:text-red-300' : 'border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300' }}"
               data-settings--nav-target="banner">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="flex-1">{{ 'settings.nav.health_banner'|trans }}</span>
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </a>
        {% endif %}

        <nav aria-label="{{ 'settings.title'|trans }}">
            <ul class="space-y-0.5">
                {% for area in navigation %}
                    {% set pages = area.pages|filter(p =>
                        (p.slug != 'ai' or aiOn or section == 'ai')
                        and (p.slug != 'health' or attention or section == 'health')
                    ) %}
                    {% if pages is not empty %}
                        <li data-settings--nav-target="area">
                            <details class="group" {{ area.key == currentArea.key ? 'open' }}>
                                <summary class="flex items-center gap-2 px-2.5 py-1.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-ink cursor-pointer select-none hover:bg-hover list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
                                    <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right w-3 text-[10px] text-ink-faint transition-transform group-open:rotate-90" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    <i class="{{ area.icon }} w-4 text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    <span class="flex-1">{{ area.labelKey|trans }}</span>
                                </summary>
                                <ul class="pl-5 pt-0.5 pb-1 space-y-0.5">
                                    {% for page in pages %}
                                        {{ _self.page(page, section, navActive, navInactive, attention) }}
                                    {% endfor %}
                                </ul>
                            </details>
                        </li>
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </nav>

        <p class="px-2.5 py-3 text-xs text-ink-muted" hidden data-settings--nav-target="empty">
            {{ 'settings.search.empty'|trans }}
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

{#
One page row and its hidden card rows. `attention` is the health report's
summary, for the badge on the Account health row.
#}
{% macro page(page, section, navActive, navInactive, attention) %}
    {% set current = section == page.slug %}
    <li data-settings--nav-target="page" data-terms="{{ page.labelKey|trans }}">
        <a href="{{ path('app_settings_page', { page: page.slug }) }}"
           class="{{ current ? navActive : navInactive }}"
           {{ current ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>
            <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate" data-settings--nav-target="label">{{ page.labelKey|trans }}</span>
            {% if page.slug == 'health' and attention %}
                {# Root causes, not symptoms — see HealthReport::indicatorCount(). #}
                <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-5 h-5 px-1.5 rounded-full text-[11px] font-semibold text-white
                             {{ attention.tone == 'danger' ? 'bg-red-500' : 'bg-amber-500' }}">
                    {{ attention.count }}
                </span>
            {% endif %}
        </a>
        <ul>
            {% for card in page.cards %}
                <li hidden data-settings--nav-target="hit"
                    data-terms="{{ card.headingKey|trans }}"
                    data-keywords="{{ card.keywordsKey ? card.keywordsKey|trans : '' }}">
                    <a href="{{ path('app_settings_page', { page: page.slug }) }}#{{ card.anchor }}"
                       class="flex flex-col pl-6 pr-2.5 py-1 rounded-md text-xs text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover">
                        <span data-settings--nav-target="label">{{ card.headingKey|trans }}</span>
                        <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint" hidden data-settings--nav-target="via"></span>
                    </a>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </li>
{% endmacro %}
